	OPERATIVE SYSTEM v6.8
STOCK-PICKING SYSTEM v6.8
CORE LOGIC
Edge = executive conviction and quality alignment at businesses the market has begun to
re-rate, sized by the weight of evidence.
Order of operations: Insiders → Quality → Momentum → Valuation
Momentum-Dependent Entry: an entry is momentum-dependent when setting the momentum
factor score to zero would cause the final composite — after all regime deductions — to fall
below the tier floor corresponding to the composite score before zeroing momentum. Complete
full scoring first, then apply this test retrospectively before finalizing override applications.
Document in journal.
HARD FLOORS — ELIMINATE BEFORE SCORING
Floor 1: CHS bottom decile OR Altman below 1.81 (capital-intensive).
Financials/REITs/utilities/asset-light tech: CHS only. If CHS unavailable and Altman inapplicable:
Piotroski ≤3 = hard floor. Document model used.
Floor 2: Negative FCF three or more consecutive years with no documented path to positive
FCF.
Floor 3: Price more than 30% below 200SMA.
