CORE CONVICTION GATE
Goal: Compute a secondary 4-factor score using the four strongest peer-reviewed predictors of
6–12 month forward returns (Price Momentum, Profitability, Earnings Quality, Post-Earnings
Drift), each using v6.7 adjusted implementations. A stock must score ≥60/100 on this gate
before composite scoring determines tier eligibility. A stock failing this gate is ineligible for entry
regardless of composite score. Threshold of 60 is provisional — live pilot review at 20 positions.
Document gate result in journal.
This gate applies to all new entries including re-entries and watchlist-triggered entries. This gate
applies to swing trades and long-term entries without exception.
EAR exemption trigger: If Factor 4 would be scored neutral (4) under v6.7 due to expiry beyond
63 trading days OR insufficient analyst coverage per v6.7 tier rules, EAR is gate-exempt and the
gate reweights equally across the remaining three factors. Document: “EAR gate-exempt —
3-factor gate applied.
