Crash Flag:
Full crash flag — both legs required:
1. 12-month momentum excess returns top decile historically
2. Market drawdown >20% from prior peak followed by >10% rebound
Full flag: −20 composite + Override 4a + tighten stops + pause Tier C momentum entries.
Existing positions when full crash flag activates: Reduce all momentum-dependent Tier A to Tier
B maximum within 5 trading days. Reduce all momentum-dependent Tier B and Tier C by 50%
within 5 trading days. Document reduction and date.
Soft crash flag — Leg 1 + ≥18% drawdown. Leg 1 is the same as full crash flag Leg 1: 12-month
momentum excess returns in the top decile historically, measured at the time of the drawdown:
−10 composite + Override 3 + Override 4b. Existing positions: trim any position sized above
composite-proportional sizing output that would result from −10 applied at entry within 10 trading
days.
Soft crash flag deactivation: Flag deactivates when BOTH conditions are met simultaneously:
(1) S&P 500 has recovered to within 5% of the prior peak that triggered the flag, AND (2) 12-1
skip-month momentum on the S&P 500 is positive. Check both conditions weekly. Document
