POSITION MANAGEMENT
Entry: 50% at initial entry. 50% on confirmation (close above entry on >1.25× 20SMA volume
within 15 calendar days). If confirmation not met by day 15: deploy second 50% only if price is
within 3% below entry and has not exceeded entry by more than 1%. If drifted >3% below entry
without stop: cancel second tranche. No gap-up entries >5% above prior close without intraday
pullback. Do not chase gaps >4% above intended entry. Both conditions apply independently.
When both gap conditions triggered simultaneously, the more restrictive governs. A gap >4%
above intended entry prohibits entry regardless of intraday pullback.
Stops: Swing: 7–8% hard stop. Long-term: 15% trailing stop OR 200SMA breach — whichever
first. Both stop types set at entry. ATR check: if 2.5× 20-day ATR implies stop greater than
maximum, reduce position size rather than truncate stop. ATR-adjusted position size =
composite-proportional size × (maximum stop type % ÷ 2.5× 20-day ATR %). Use 7% swing
maximum and 15% long-term maximum. Document ATR-adjusted size and ATR value.
Whipsaw Re-Entry: Minimum 5 trading days after stop-out. Full checklist required. Swing
re-entries: 15-day earnings gate applies without exception. Long-term re-entries within 10
calendar days of earnings: reduce initial size to 25% until post-earnings confirmation. Voluntary
exit: minimum 1 trading day before re-entry same ticker.
